WEBVTT

1
00:00:13.041 --> 00:00:16.484
rubbed her hands together and thought about doing a Uniting spell.

2
00:00:17.165 --> 00:00:21.849
But her head was spinning with what she had just realized, and she couldn't focus on what she

3
00:00:21.889 --> 00:00:22.790
was trying to do.

4
00:00:23.610 --> 00:00:28.455
It was amazing to think that she and Zann were living through some of the Magica history she

5
00:00:28.515 --> 00:00:29.736
found so fascinating.

6
00:00:30.580 --> 00:00:35.902
"Hardly anyone in Magica knows what the world was like this far in the past," she thought.

7
00:00:35.922 --> 00:00:38.562
"Now Zann and I will be able to tell them."

8
00:00:39.463 --> 00:00:41.183
She gulped, realizing something.

9
00:00:41.203 --> 00:00:46.885
"Well if we can figure out how to get back to our own time, that is!"

10
00:00:46.905 --> 00:00:48.285
"What's wrong?"

11
00:00:48.885 --> 00:00:50.786
Zann squeezed her arm impatiently.

12
00:00:50.806 --> 00:00:53.627
"Are you going to do the Uniting spell, or what?"

13
00:00:54.367 --> 00:00:55.927
"Um, sorry," Perda said.

14
00:00:55.947 --> 00:00:58.548
"Please zap us back to the village, okay?

15
00:00:59.200 --> 00:01:03.341
I'm sure that's where they went, so we don't need to do the Uniting spell.

16
00:01:03.942 --> 00:01:05.782
I'll help create friction for the Zap."

17
00:01:06.482 --> 00:01:09.323
"Okay," Zann said, looking slightly confused.

18
00:01:09.864 --> 00:01:13.065
He held on tightly to Perda's arm, and also to Zing.

19
00:01:13.085 --> 00:01:16.226
"Zap!" Splash!

20
00:01:17.166 --> 00:01:22.608
They landed in a clear, cold stream bubbling through a pretty meadow in the foothills of the mountains.

21
00:01:23.276 --> 00:01:29.282
Birds were chirping all around, and Perda couldn't help wondering how many species she would recognize from her

22
00:01:29.342 --> 00:01:29.902
own time.

23
00:01:29.922 --> 00:01:32.965
"It's too bad Darb isn't with us," she said.

24
00:01:32.985 --> 00:01:36.488
"He would have recognized more of the plants and animals here.

25
00:01:37.229 --> 00:01:39.471
Maybe we would have figured things out faster."

26
00:01:39.491 --> 00:01:41.453
"Maybe," Zann said.

27
00:01:41.473 --> 00:01:43.314
"But you figured it out anyway.

28
00:01:43.935 --> 00:01:45.076
I'm not sure I would have."

29
00:01:46.177 --> 00:01:47.218
Perda smiled at him.

30
00:01:47.238 --> 00:01:52.069
"We can rest here for a few minutes," she said as they stepped out of the water and

31
00:01:52.149 --> 00:01:53.529
magically dried their shoes.

32
00:01:53.549 --> 00:02:00.931
"Now that Vilkor knows Mellis isn't on his side, he's probably doing the zapping himself.

33
00:02:01.632 --> 00:02:04.933
He's not as strong as she is, so he'll have to rest too."

34
00:02:05.733 --> 00:02:10.134
She flopped onto the ground, still thinking about everything she'd just figured out.

35
00:02:10.854 --> 00:02:15.556
Mentioning Mellis made her think again about how powerful their new friend's magic was.

36
00:02:16.276 --> 00:02:22.900
She appeared to have nearly as much magical ability as an experienced Magic Master like Zann's grandfather, Boz.

37
00:02:22.920 --> 00:02:28.163
"It all makes sense now," Perda said thoughtfully.

38
00:02:28.183 --> 00:02:34.346
"If that's really the Wormwood tree, and Mellis opened the Source of magic, then it's no wonder she's

39
00:02:34.386 --> 00:02:36.187
got super strong magic energy.

40
00:02:37.068 --> 00:02:42.411
She was completely surrounded by it when it first emerged in its purest form."

41
00:02:43.091 --> 00:02:44.212
Zann looked interested.

42
00:02:44.796 --> 00:02:47.158
"So the energy was more concentrated, right?"

43
00:02:47.478 --> 00:02:47.859
he said.

44
00:02:47.879 --> 00:02:48.839
"I get it.

45
00:02:49.320 --> 00:02:51.181
That's probably why she fainted at first.

46
00:02:51.802 --> 00:02:54.504
It overwhelmed her since she wasn't used to magic at all.

47
00:02:55.305 --> 00:02:58.407
But maybe it's also why she's so good at magic now."

48
00:02:58.427 --> 00:03:04.032
"Right." Perda glanced at Mount Mystery, now a dark peak in the distance.

49
00:03:04.052 --> 00:03:10.257
"It's weird to think about all the stuff we've seen here and compare it to our own time."

50
00:03:10.277 --> 00:03:13.820
"Yeah, I was thinking about that while we zapped," Zann said.

51
00:03:14.400 --> 00:03:18.642
"The mine where Krub made me work is probably where the spellstone mines are in our time."

52
00:03:19.782 --> 00:03:20.543
Perda nodded.

53
00:03:20.983 --> 00:03:24.164
They had visited those mines a couple of times on school trips.

54
00:03:24.884 --> 00:03:27.445
Spellstones were another relic of the Old Times.

55
00:03:28.026 --> 00:03:33.368
They didn't contain much power in modern times, but during the Old Times, they'd been important for different

56
00:03:33.408 --> 00:03:34.248
kinds of magic.

57
00:03:34.268 --> 00:03:36.329
"Let's zap again," she said.

58
00:03:36.349 --> 00:03:38.950
"I don't want to let Vilkor get a head start.

59
00:03:39.510 --> 00:03:40.511
Are you rested enough?"

60
00:03:41.311 --> 00:03:43.292
"Sure," Zann said with a smile.

61
00:03:43.736 --> 00:03:45.797
"Are you sure you don't want to zap us this time?

62
00:03:46.318 --> 00:03:48.219
We've already landed in the water once."

63
00:03:49.199 --> 00:03:50.220
"It's okay—you do it."

64
00:03:50.760 --> 00:03:54.543
Perda still felt distracted by all the thoughts running through her head.

65
00:03:56.584 --> 00:04:00.907
The next zap brought them to a flat area with only a few trees and shrubs.

66
00:04:01.447 --> 00:04:05.189
There was no water around, either, so their shoes stayed dry this time.

67
00:04:05.710 --> 00:04:08.992
However, Zann accidentally landed them in a prickly bush.

68
00:04:09.684 --> 00:04:15.527
"I'm still trying to figure out which sites in this time correspond with landmarks in our own time,"

69
00:04:16.228 --> 00:04:18.949
Perda said as she healed the scratches from the thorns.

70
00:04:18.969 --> 00:04:26.714
"If the area by the well eventually turns into Wormwood, that means First City will be created all

71
00:04:26.774 --> 00:04:29.035
across Mellis and Vilkor's farm."

72
00:04:29.055 --> 00:04:33.798
"You're probably right," Zann agreed, flopping down on the grass to rest.

73
00:04:34.398 --> 00:04:37.460
He shooed away Zing, who was breathing smoke into his face.

74
00:04:38.036 --> 00:04:42.319
"But First City is so big, it probably stretches as far as their village too.

75
00:04:43.139 --> 00:04:44.620
I wonder where the palace will be?

76
00:04:45.220 --> 00:04:46.321
Maybe we can figure it out."

77
00:04:46.341 --> 00:04:48.923
"Maybe." Perda shrugged.

78
00:04:48.943 --> 00:04:51.404
"We'd better not wait too long to zap again.

79
00:04:52.124 --> 00:04:57.368
If we get to the village before Vilkor does, maybe we can figure out a plan to rescue

80
00:04:57.428 --> 00:04:59.609
Mellis before they find Zira."

81
00:04:59.629 --> 00:05:01.850
"Good idea," Zann said.

82
00:05:01.870 --> 00:05:04.452
"I'm not looking forward to seeing Zira again.

83
00:05:05.128 --> 00:05:08.149
Last time we saw her, she tried to take me prisoner!"

84
00:05:08.749 --> 00:05:10.189
Perda realized he was right.

85
00:05:10.209 --> 00:05:12.010
"We'll have to be careful."

86
00:05:12.790 --> 00:05:13.370
She smiled.

87
00:05:13.390 --> 00:05:15.931
"Which means I'll do the zapping this time.

88
00:05:16.451 --> 00:05:18.672
Otherwise we might land right in her lap!"

89
00:05:19.492 --> 00:05:20.852
Zann laughed sheepishly.

90
00:05:20.872 --> 00:05:23.953
"Okay. Come here, Zing.

91
00:05:24.233 --> 00:05:24.613
Let's go!"

92
00:05:25.213 --> 00:05:28.854
Perda grabbed Zann's arm, and then waited for him to catch Zing.

93
00:05:29.575 --> 00:05:34.136
She created friction, took a deep breath, and focused on where she wanted to go.

94
00:05:34.924 --> 00:05:37.005
"I'll aim for the farmhouse," she said.

95
00:05:37.025 --> 00:05:44.408
"Now that Vilkor has his fancy mansion in town, there probably won't be anyone at the farm."

96
00:05:45.309 --> 00:05:46.509
She took a deep breath.

97
00:05:46.529 --> 00:05:55.913
"Zap!" When they landed, the first thing Perda saw was the farmhouse right beside them, which made her

98
00:05:55.993 --> 00:05:58.494
glad they'd landed where she'd wanted to land.

99
00:05:58.954 --> 00:06:02.770
But the second thing she saw was "Gorzogs!"

100
00:06:02.790 --> 00:06:07.608
Zann shouted, yanking Perda aside just as one of the fearsome creatures leaped at her.
